{"id":"texplate","name":"TeXplate","aliases":[],"caption":"A tool for creating document structures based on templates","authors":[{"id":"cereda","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Island of TeX","year":"2021"}],"license":"bsd3","version":{"number":"1.0.6","date":""},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      TeXplate is a tool for creating document structures based on templates.\n      The application name is a word play on <em>TeX<\u002fem> and <em>template<\u002fem>,\n      so the purpose seems quite obvious: we want to provide an easy and\n      straightforward framework for reducing the typical code boilerplate\n      when writing TeX documents.\n      Also note that one can easily extrapolate the use beyond articles\n      and theses: the application is powerful enough to generate\n      <em>any<\u002fem> text-based structure, given that\n      a corresponding template exists.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/support/texplate/README.md"},{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/support/texplate/doc/texplate-manual.pdf"}],"bugs":"https://gitlab.com/islandoftex/texplate/-/work_items","repository":"https://gitlab.com/islandoftex/texplate","ctan":{"path":"/support/texplate","file":true},"install":"/support/texplate.tds.zip","miktex":"texplate","texlive":"texplate","topics":["gentex","doc-templ","doc-gen"]}